  // song plays this chord (root + family); it is what the colour is derived
  // from, so the label and the tint can never disagree.
  // `n` = how many times the whole SONG plays this chord (chart_model builds
  // it as the observable the confidence percentage stands for). Until
  // 2026-08-17 the chord objects the shell builds never copied it, so `ch.n`
  // was undefined everywhere and the editor announced "played once in this
  // song" over every chord of every chart — including a C the song plays
  // twenty-four times. No count on the chart (the `retour_*` ones carry none)
