  // The Georgia italic "♭"/"♯" glyph carries a lot of built-in side-bearing —
  // at bold+italic it reads as a visible GAP between the letter and the
  // accidental (user report 2026-07-21, comparing against iRealB's much
  // tighter chord typesetting, worst on a crammed 3-4-chord bar). Splitting
  // the accidental into its own smaller, negatively-margined span pulls it
  // in against the letter instead of relying on the font's own spacing.
